yoyo init, doctor, update and help now refuse arguments they don't accept, with exit 2. yoyo init zzz no longer creates YOYO.md. It's committed as e34811da, titled "Part of #982".

What I measured first (fresh temp dir, stdin from /dev/null): doctor zzz, update zzz, help zzz and init zzz all exited 0, and init zzz wrote YOYO.md. Bare doctor exits 0, so that's the near-miss I pinned.

What changed (in src/dispatch_sub.rs, using Day 232's refuse_stray_arg and positional_after_verb, not a second code path):
• `init`: a stray argument is refused before anything is written. Bare yoyo init still writes YOYO.md.
• `doctor`: only reads --provider and --model. Those still work, and anything else positional exits 2.
• `update`: takes no argument. The refusal happens before any network call, so the test never goes online.
• `help`: the shell yoyo help took no argument, but the REPL has /help <command>. Refusing every argument would have turned yoyo help status from exit 0 into exit 2. So yoyo help <command> now prints the same text as /help <command>, and an unknown topic like yoyo help zzz exits 2 and names it, as git help zzz and cargo help zzz also reject it. One difference from the REPL: the shell version doesn't look up custom commands.

Tests: init_doctor_update_and_help_refuse_what_they_do_not_accept in tests/integration.rs runs the real binary in a temp dir:
• init zzz, doctor zzz and update zzz exit 2 with nothing on stdout, and YOYO.md is absent afterwards.
• help zzz exits 2, and help status exits 0.
• Bare help, bare doctor and doctor with its flags still exit 0, and bare init still writes the file.

For a positive control I temporarily removed init's refusal. The test failed on ["init","zzz"] (exit 0, expected 2), and passed again once I put it back. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and fmt are all green.

Also updated: the size register in tests/module_size.rs (src/dispatch_sub.rs 2503 → 2521) and two spots in docs/src/usage/commands.md: the exit-code paragraph and the yoyo help [command] table row.

Still open on #982: config show still exits 0 when .yoyo.toml can't be read, and health zzz still ignores its argument. I listed both, with the sha, in a comment on #982. The issue stays open.
